# {{title}}

This native Qt 6 Widgets application was generated with `gansi create`.
The small `build.rs` retains CXX-Qt dependency initializers in the final
executable; it does not contain or generate application-owned C++ code.
It requires Rust 1.89 or newer.

## Requirements

Fedora:

```sh
sudo dnf install qt6-qtbase-devel gcc-c++ cmake ninja-build pkgconf-pkg-config
```

Ubuntu:

```sh
sudo apt install qt6-base-dev g++ cmake ninja-build pkg-config
```

## Run

```sh
gansi doctor  # diagnose Rust, C++, CMake, and Qt
gansi run     # build and run the app
gansi test    # run tests
gansi analyze # run Clippy with warnings denied
gansi format --check
gansi upgrade # update Cargo.lock
gansi add serde -- --features derive
gansi build   # build a release bundle under dist/
```

On Linux, run the bundle through `dist/{{name}}/{{name}}`. Its launcher selects
the bundled Qt libraries and plugins while leaving glibc and graphics drivers
to the target system. `gansi build` also emits a `.tar.gz` containing that
directory plus `SHA256SUMS` for transfer verification. Package integration
inputs live under `share/`: a valid desktop entry and scalable application
icon. Change their generated identifiers, summary, category, and artwork before
release as appropriate.

`gansi create` records the detected Qt version, compiler family, and host
architecture in `gansi.toml`. Project commands reject a mismatched environment
instead of silently building with a different toolchain; update a pin only as
an intentional SDK/toolchain migration. Set `deployment.bundle_name` and replace
the `com.example.*` `deployment.app_id` before producing real packages; bundle
desktop metadata is rendered from those values.

For a display-free smoke run:

```sh
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen YSE_SMOKE=1 gansi run
```

For release packaging, see [`RELEASE.md`](RELEASE.md).

## CI before Yse is published

The generated `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs formatting, Clippy, tests, and an
offscreen Qt interaction smoke on Ubuntu. Because this project initially
records an absolute path to your local Yse checkout, the workflow checks out
`xiaoshihou514/yse` into the job and replaces that path before building. Pin
the Yse checkout to a release tag or commit when you need reproducible CI, and
replace the path dependency with the crates.io release after publication.
macOS is intentionally not included until that path is tested on a real host.
